Subject: Landlock: unavailable without fork

Landlock is applied in a forked child that keeps running Ruby. On a Ruby whose fork is not implemented
(respond_to?(:fork) is false, as MRI reports for rb_f_notimplement methods; a compiled brew is one) report
:missing_fork, so brew runs the step unsandboxed with its usual warning instead of failing in safe_fork.
---
diff --git a/Library/Homebrew/extend/os/linux/sandbox/landlock.rb b/Library/Homebrew/extend/os/linux/sandbox/landlock.rb
index 94a6aba359..369b1f313d 100644
--- a/Library/Homebrew/extend/os/linux/sandbox/landlock.rb
+++ b/Library/Homebrew/extend/os/linux/sandbox/landlock.rb
@@ -137,6 +137,8 @@ class Sandbox
           "Landlock cannot be used because Linux sandboxing is disabled."
         when :missing_fiddle
           "Landlock requires Ruby's bundled Fiddle library."
+        when :missing_fork
+          "Landlock requires a Ruby that implements fork."
         when :unsupported
           "Landlock is not supported by this Linux kernel."
         when :disabled
@@ -253,6 +255,8 @@ class Sandbox
         rescue LoadError
           return :missing_fiddle
         end
+        # Landlock is applied in a forked child, which needs a Ruby that implements fork.
+        return :missing_fork unless Process.respond_to?(:fork)
 
         version = kernel_abi_version
         if version
